        "question": "Can a brain injury cause changes in the personality of the individual?",
        "answer": "Changes in behaviour, mood, or personality are recognised as a genuine effect of brain injury. An injury can impact those areas of the brain that are responsible for regulating emotions and behaviour. This is the reason why proper rehabilitation is needed, which may ensure support from psychology to neuropsychology."
