        "question": "Should I be using my thumb in case I have thumb base osteoarthritis?",
        "answer": "You generally don’t need to stop using your thumb. Avoiding hand use completely is not very helpful because strength around the joint needs to be maintained. Performing normal activities is fine; however, aggravating activities like gripping or heavy pinching need modification."
