        "question": "Can a trigger point pain cause pain somewhere else?",
        "answer": "Yes. Sometimes, trigger points produce referred pain, which happens when pressing or loading one part of a muscle reproduces pain in another location. This is the reason why the location of the pain does not always identify the source."
